      "why": "the portrait  (mobile) crop needs an ink scrim at alpha 0.852 for --fg-muted to clear 4.5:1, so UNDER THE TEXT this frame is barely visible — above 0.85 it always is, and no grade changes that (the composite ceiling under a glyph is fixed; see SHARP_TONE for the arithmetic). What decides whether the hero reads as a photograph is the APERTURE — the text-free regions where the veil is thin — not this number. Check it in components/site/hero-scrim.module.css and in check-hero-contrast's VISIBILITY table before reaching for a darker crop or a heavier grade."
